# for Loop

Go has only **one** loop construct: `for`. However, `for` can be used in several styles.

## 1. C-Style for (init; condition; post)

```go
for i := 0; i < 5; i++ {
    fmt.Println(i)
}
// Output: 0 1 2 3 4

// Counting down
for i := 10; i > 0; i -= 2 {
    fmt.Print(i, " ")  // 10 8 6 4 2
}
```

## 2. While-Style (condition only)

```go
n := 1
for n < 100 {
    n *= 2
}
fmt.Println(n) // 128
```

## 3. Infinite Loop

```go
for {
    fmt.Println("Loop forever!")
    // Must have break or return to exit
    break
}
```

## `break` — Stop the Loop

```go
for i := 0; i < 10; i++ {
    if i == 5 {
        break  // exit loop when i == 5
    }
    fmt.Print(i, " ")  // 0 1 2 3 4
}
```

## `continue` — Skip an Iteration

```go
for i := 0; i < 10; i++ {
    if i%2 != 0 {
        continue  // skip odd numbers
    }
    fmt.Print(i, " ")  // 0 2 4 6 8
}
```

## `goto` — Jump to a Label

```go
// goto is rarely used and generally avoided
func main() {
    i := 0
loop:
    if i < 3 {
        fmt.Println(i)
        i++
        goto loop
    }
}
```

## Labels for Nested Loops

Labels are useful for `break` and `continue` on nested loops:

```go
outer:
    for i := 0; i < 3; i++ {
        for j := 0; j < 3; j++ {
            if j == 1 {
                continue outer  // skip to next iteration of outer loop
            }
            fmt.Printf("(%d,%d) ", i, j)
        }
    }
// Output: (0,0) (1,0) (2,0)

func findPair() {
outer:
    for i := 0; i < 5; i++ {
        for j := 0; j < 5; j++ {
            if i+j == 6 {
                fmt.Printf("Pair: (%d, %d)\n", i, j)
                break outer  // exit all loops!
            }
        }
    }
}
```

## Summary of All Forms

```go
// C-style
for init; condition; post { }

// While-style
for condition { }

// Infinite
for { }

// Range (covered in next lesson)
for index, value := range collection { }
```

| Style | When to Use |
|---|---|
| C-style | When you need a custom index or step |
| While-style | When a condition alone is sufficient |
| Infinite | Server loop, event loop |
| Range | Iterating collections (slice, map, string) |

starterCode:
package main

import "fmt"

func main() {
	// C-style: cetak tabel kuadrat
	fmt.Println("Tabel kuadrat:")
	for i := 1; i <= 5; i++ {
		fmt.Printf("%d^2 = %d\n", i, i*i)
	}

	// While-style: cari pangkat 2 pertama > 1000
	n := 1
	for n <= 1000 {
		n *= 2
	}
	fmt.Println("\nPangkat 2 pertama > 1000:", n)

	// continue: cetak hanya bilangan habis dibagi 3
	fmt.Println("\nBilangan habis dibagi 3 (1-20):")
	for i := 1; i <= 20; i++ {
		if i%3 != 0 {
			continue
		}
		fmt.Print(i, " ")
	}
	fmt.Println()

	// Labels: cari pasangan pertama yang jumlahnya 7
	fmt.Println("\nPasangan pertama yang berjumlah 7:")
outer:
	for i := 1; i <= 5; i++ {
		for j := 1; j <= 5; j++ {
			if i+j == 7 {
				fmt.Printf("(%d + %d = 7)\n", i, j)
				break outer
			}
		}
	}
}
